    "body": "Fixes #3037\n\n## Summary\n\nTwo problems in `Retrying`, both visible on `main` (96f33fa):\n\n1. **The first retry waited `wait_seconds × base × (1 + jitter)`**, because the delay was multiplied *before* the sleep. With the `ApiModel` defaults (`wait_seconds=60`, `base=2`) that means 120–240s between attempt 1 and 2 instead of ~60s.\n2. **`Retry-After` was ignored entirely.** A 429 asking for 3 seconds still blocked the call for the exponential schedule's delay (minutes with the defaults).\n\n## Change\n\n```python\nsleep_seconds = delay                    # configured wait is the first sleep\nretry_after = _retry_after_seconds(e)\nif retry_after is not None:\n    sleep_seconds = max(sleep_seconds, retry_after)   # never sleep less than asked\ndelay *= self.exponential_base * (1 + self.jitter * random.random())  # applies to the next wait\n...\ntime.sleep(sleep_seconds)\n```\n\n`_retry_after_seconds()` reads the numeric form of `Retry-After` from `error.response.headers` when the exception carries an HTTP response, and returns `None` otherwise. The HTTP-date form is deliberately ignored rather than guessed at; a malformed/missing header falls back to the configured schedule, and a header can only lengthen the wait, never shorten it.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew `TestRetryingSchedule` in `tests/test_utils.py` (monkeypatches `smolagents.utils.time.sleep`, so no real sleeping):\n\n- first retry sleeps exactly `wait_seconds`;\n- subsequent waits follow `wait_seconds, 2×, 4×` with `jitter=False`;\n- a `Retry-After: 7` header makes the wait 7s even when `wait_seconds=1`;\n- a `Retry-After: 1` header does not shorten a configured 10s wait;\n- an HTTP-date `Retry-After` is ignored (falls back to `wait_seconds`).\n",
